            <p class="font-semibold text-black text-xl">
                Four-time Grammy-nominated pop artist and singer-songwriter Bebe Rexha has gone indie and entered a partnership with powerhouse Bay Area-based label and distributor EMPIRE.
            </p>

            <p>
                The deal marks a significant moment for both artists and the independent music landscape. Rexha, known for hits like "Meant to Be" and "I'm Good (Blue)," brings her massive commercial appeal to the independent sector, proving that major success doesn't require a major label.
            </p>

            <h2>A New Chapter</h2>
            <p>
                "I've always believed in the power of independence," Rexha said in a statement. "EMPIRE understands my vision and gives me the freedom to create on my own terms while providing the infrastructure to reach a global audience."
            </p>

            <p>
                The partnership will see EMPIRE handling distribution, marketing, and publishing for Rexha's future releases, while the artist maintains ownership of her masters and creative control.
            </p>

            <div class="bg-gray-100 rounded-xl p-8 my-8 border-l-4 border-black">
                <p class="italic text-gray-700 mb-4">"Bebe is a game-changer. Her decision to go independent sends a powerful message to the industry."</p>
                <p class="font-bold text-sm">— Ghazi Shami, CEO of EMPIRE</p>
            </div>

            <h2>The EMPIRE Model</h2>
            <p>
                EMPIRE has built a reputation as one of the most successful independent labels in the world, with a roster that includes Tyga, Fireboy DML, and K Camp. Their artist-friendly approach has disrupted traditional label structures.
            </p>

            <p>
                The company offers transparent royalty splits, faster payment cycles, and retains none of the artist's masters—an increasingly attractive proposition in today's music economy.
            </p>

            <h2>What's Next</h2>
            <p>
                Rexha is expected to release her first single under the EMPIRE banner in early 2025, with a full album to follow. The announcement has already generated significant buzz across social media platforms.
            </p>

            <p>
